      "conflict_note": {
        "decision_id": "P33-DECISION-CLASS-C-ROAD-COUNTY-RECONCILIATION-2026-09-18",
        "conflict_type": "value_disagreement",
        "confidence": "high",
        "summary": "A competing candidate value was investigated and rejected: World Bank/ESMAP \"Kenya - Roads\" spatial derivation (energydata.info, KRB-attributed, ~2017 vintage) suggested 345.8 km, but failed the required reconciliation check against the official value. The official value published here was retained; the rejected candidate was not published as a probable value.",
        "rationale": "The reconciliation condition ('reconcile additive totals where meaningful') fails decisively and non-uniformly, not merely by an acceptable rounding/vintage margin. This means the 'C'-prefixed RID_8 codes in the only publicly downloadable classified road GIS layer found do not correspond reliably to KeRRA's current official Class C classification underlying KNBS Table 11.9. Building a constituency breakdown on this input would misrepresent individual constituencies by up to an order of magnitude (worst case, two orders of magnitude for Nairobi), which is precisely the kind of fabricated-precision outcome the Atlas's anti-fabrication rule exists to prevent. No defensible spatial_derivation is currently possible for this indicator at constituency level.",
        "source_contract": "data/p31/source/class-c-road-spatial-derivation-attempt.json"
      }
